Subject: [PATCH 23/28] MIDI/gate output timer: count from 0 at every start

The compare match clears TCNT_2, but it keeps counting until the interrupt
stops the timer, which can be hundreds of counts later while
Song::renderAudio() masks interrupts (up to 451 in the emulator). The next
start counted on from there: that run fired as much early (up to 38 samples),
or, with a TGRA below the leftover, only after the 16-bit counter wrapped,
about 127 ms late (seen while saving: timer runs up to 5408 samples late in
the base). Now TCNT is set to 0 before the timer is started.

In the emulator with the counter modelled (tests/song MIDI=1), the timer as
scheduled against the DMA reaching the window's sample: normal playback 192
runs, saving 97 runs, all within -1.4 ... +0.2 samples, leftover 0 at every
start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
---
 src/deluge/processing/engines/audio_engine.cpp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/deluge/processing/engines/audio_engine.cpp b/src/deluge/processing/engines/audio_engine.cpp
index 63b023ad..f354d09f 100644
--- a/src/deluge/processing/engines/audio_engine.cpp
+++ b/src/deluge/processing/engines/audio_engine.cpp
@@ -1171,6 +1171,11 @@ void scheduleMidiGateOutISR(uint32_t saddrPosAtStart, int32_t unadjustedNumSampl
 
 		// Set delay time. This is samplesTilMIDIOrGate * 515616 / kSampleRate.
 		*TGRA[TIMER_MIDI_GATE_OUTPUT] = ((uint32_t)samplesTilMIDIOrGate * 766245) >> 16;
+		// mastertune-v13: count from 0. The compare match clears the counter, but it goes on counting until the
+		// interrupt stops the timer, which can be hundreds of counts later while Song::renderAudio() has interrupts
+		// masked. Left there, the next run fired that much early, or, with a delay shorter than the leftover, only
+		// after the 16-bit counter wrapped round (about 127 ms late)
+		*TCNT[TIMER_MIDI_GATE_OUTPUT] = 0;
 		enableTimer(TIMER_MIDI_GATE_OUTPUT);
 	}
 }
